{
  "schema": "orca.head_envelope.v1",
  "id": "bambu-a1-nozzle-06",
  "name": "Bambu Lab A1 (0.6 mm nozzle; stock hotend and segmented ducts)",
  "provenance": "Floor: BambuStudio A1 / A1 mini machine presets set nozzle_height = 4.76 mm, the height below which Bambu's own clearance model has nothing but the nozzle, at most 4 mm across (MAX_OUTER_NOZZLE_DIAMETER): https://github.com/bambulab/BambuStudio/tree/47a13eeb1d9af65ef2371e361c856e21d4f6ca72/resources/profiles/BBL/machine . Sock and duct outlets start there. Community report of the A1 mini part cooler about 6.5 mm above the bed while printing (https://forum.bambulab.com/t/spacing-needed-when-using-by-object-printing-is-too-conservative/99336) agrees within the duct's slope; 4.76 is kept as the lower, published bound. Nozzle: 0.6 mm land and 35-degree half-angle cone of the Bambu hotend CAD (https://www.printables.com/model/533213 Hotend.STEP, X1/P1; the A1 hotend is the same nozzle family, both 47.3 mm long per Bambu's store listings), to the 4 mm envelope at Z=2.48, then a 4 mm cylinder to Z=4.76. Sock: lower skirt radius 4.5 to Z=6.5, then half-widths 9/7 enclosing the ceramic heater to Z=24. Ducts, from OEM toolhead photos (https://wiki.bambulab.com/en/a1-mini/maintenance/toolhead , front image /n1/a1-mini-print-head/toolhead.jpg at 0.317 mm/pixel, 52 mm duct width from https://www.printables.com/model/685475): outlets X=+-8..24, Y=+-8; outer walls X=+-24..26 from Z=6; risers X=+-8..26, Y=+-15 from Z=9; cover Z=23. Shared toolhead: https://wiki.bambulab.com/en/a1/manual/faq . BambuStudio A1 / A1 mini gantry underside 25 mm, farther edge 56.5 mm: symmetric Y span +-56.5, infinite X. Body axial/lateral margins 0.3 mm. Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Derived 2026-10-12; calibrated=false. Nozzle variant: 0.6 mm bore with a 0.8 mm land diameter, keeping the CAD 0.4 mm bore/0.6 mm land radial wall of 0.1 mm. Retain the 35-degree cone half-angle, capped at the same shoulder radius (2 mm on A1, 1.55 mm on P1S); expand the finite lower cone boxes to enclose it. All other hotend, housing and gantry dimensions and 0.3 mm body margins are unchanged. Selected nozzle estimate 2026-10-12.",
